# L §4.4 "One rule for every window a line meets": "A read whose value depends on where in a window the day falls is
# a hole, HOLE-IMPRECISE, unless the line states windows each", which "prints one line per maximal sub-window ... over
# which the answer is constant": e = one_of([03-02, 03-09]) gives a line per day (q1); "A text that takes a window as
# one day pins it to that day with a with pin (§5.18), which the register prints (pinned:, §8.2)": d pinned to
# 2020-07-31 is not before 2020-07-15 (q2); "A comparison is decided when the whole interval lies on one side": e is
# before 2020-03-10 on both days (q3). (Writer 8: windows latest, windows earliest, latest() and earliest() are gone.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

input d: date
input e: date

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  d = window(2020-07-01, 2020-07-31)
  e = one_of([2020-03-02, 2020-03-09])

ask q1: e windows each
ask q2: d < 2020-07-15 with d = 2020-07-31
ask q3: e < 2020-03-10
=== expect
q1 [e = 2020-03-02]: 2020-03-02
  cut 2026-12-31
q1 [e = 2020-03-09]: 2020-03-09
  cut 2026-12-31
q2: false
  pinned: d = 2020-07-31
  cut 2026-12-31
q3: true
  cut 2026-12-31
